  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 20
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: The liberated iodine immediately reacts with the thiosulphate ions
    to form iodide and tetrathionate ions. lodine undergoes which of the following
    reactions?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: The time taken by iodine to consume all the thiosulphate ions
    in the solution is reproducible, and the time taken for the appearance of blue
    colour is noted. Reproducibility is the ability to implement the experimental
    procedures as exactly as possible to obtain the same results.
  options:
  - Oxidation
  - Reduciton
  - Redox Reaction
  - None Of the above
  correctOptionIndex: 1
